                <pb facs="0241" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg141"/>

                <head>No. 92.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morton to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 6, 1884.</date>
                        (Received February 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 495.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your telegram received the 2d
                    ultimo, informing me that the Commercial Cable Company had obtained permission
                    to land on the coast of the United States, and requesting me to ask that the
                    same privilege be given to the company in France, I have the honor to state that
                    this application has been made and granted.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LEVI P. MORTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
